          "returnType": null,
          "description": "Estimated resident bytes over every ready asset. The loader cannot see inside a type's resource, so payloads are sized by shape: binary buffers and blobs by their length, strings by their UTF-16 length, decoded audio by its PCM footprint, and anything carrying pixel dimensions at four bytes per texel. A structured payload (parsed JSON, an XML document, a font face) contributes nothing, and GPU-side copies are not counted at all - read RenderStats.gpuMemoryBytes for those. Treat this as a floor on CPU-side asset memory, not an accounting of it."
        },
